>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `filter_rewrites`

``` hol4
simpLib.filter_rewrites :
  ((simpLib.thname option * thm) -> bool) ->
  simpLib.simpset -> simpLib.simpset
simpLib.filter_rewrites_preserving_controls :
  ((simpLib.thname option * thm) -> bool) ->
  simpLib.simpset -> simpLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes the rewrites of a simpset that a predicate rejects.

`filter_rewrites keep ss` removes every rewrite `(name, th)`, as it was
added to `ss`, for which `keep` returns false. AC rewrites (`AC`, or a
fragment's `ac` field) are always kept and not shown to `keep`. Everything
else in `ss` is kept, including its exclusions, limit, rewrite maker,
solvers and loopers, which rebuilding from `ssfrags_of ss` would lose. If
nothing is rejected, `ss` itself is returned.

The simpset is rebuilt, so bounded rewrites (`Once`, `Ntimes`) start again
with their full number of uses. With `filter_rewrites_preserving_controls`
they keep the number of uses they had left.

### Failure

Fails if `keep` fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>> fun keep (_, th) = not (aconv (concl th) (concl AND_CLAUSES));
>>_ val ss = simpLib.filter_rewrites keep
     boolSimps.bool_ss;
>> QCONV (simpLib.SIMP_CONV ss []) “p ∧ T”;
>> simpLib.SIMP_CONV ss [] “p ∨ F”;
```

